# Patient Dashboard UI

When editing the patient dashboard (`PatientDashboard.jsx`, `PatientChartHeader`, tabs, checkout, intake, etc.), prioritize **clinical clarity over density**. The page should feel calm, scannable, and trustworthy — not overloaded.

## Layout & hierarchy

- **Chrome** (header + encounter bar + tabs): fixed structure; content scrolls below.
- **Header**: 2–3 visual zones max — identity (photo, name, MRN, encounter #), quick demographics (phone, email, address), and alert chips (allergies, insurance, care team, emergency contact).
- **Tab content**: one primary action per section; use cards with clear titles and short descriptions.
- **Whitespace**: prefer `gap-4`/`gap-6` between sections; avoid stacking 6+ dense blocks without grouping.
- **Grid**: use responsive grids (`sm:grid-cols-2`, `lg:grid-cols-3`) — never cram 4+ columns of text on mobile.

## Color coding (semantic, consistent)

Use only the five clinical tones from `@/lib/statusColors` / CSS classes `status-soft-*`:

| Meaning | Tone | Treatment |
|---------|------|-----------|
| Allergies / critical alerts | danger | Soft danger badge, left border `border-l-4 border-destructive` |
| Active encounter / in progress | info | Soft info badge or primary accent |
| Completed / verified | success | Soft success badge |
| Pending / due / needs attention | warning | Soft warning badge |
| Draft / inactive / self-pay | muted | Soft muted badge |
| Destructive actions | danger | `variant="destructive"` only for irreversible actions |

Reuse design tokens (`primary`, `success`, `warning`, `info`, `destructive`, `muted`) — do not invent purple/orange/cyan/rainbow status colors.

## Components & buttons

- Use shadcn `Button`, `Badge`, `Card`, `Tabs` — match patterns from `EncountersPage` and `PatientsPage`.
- **Primary button**: one per card/section (main action). Secondary actions: `variant="outline"` or `ghost`.
- **Icon buttons**: always include `aria-label`.
- **Tables**: zebra optional; status as colored `Badge`, not raw text.
- **Empty states**: icon + one-line message + optional CTA — never a bare "—".

## Reduce overload

- Collapse secondary detail into tooltips, popovers, or "View more" — e.g. emergency contact on hover.
- Group related fields in labeled **info tiles** (icon + label + value), not long label:value paragraphs.
- Long forms: use stepped sections or accordion cards, not one scrolling wall.
- Tab badges: only for counts that need attention (pending orders, unsigned notes).

## Typography

- Section titles: `text-base font-semibold` inside cards; page title only in header.
- Labels: `text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground`.
- Values: `text-sm font-medium text-foreground`.
- Monospace for MRN, encounter #, codes only.

## Do not

- Add new dependencies for styling.
- Duplicate patient demographics in every tab — link back to header/profile.
- Use more than 2 font weights per section.
- Return `null` for empty chart/header — show skeleton, error, or guided empty state.

## Reference files

- Shell: `PatientDashboard.jsx`, `PatientChartHeader.jsx`, `PatientChartEncounterBar.jsx`
- Patterns: `checkout/CheckoutWorkspace.jsx`, `PatientSummaryTab.jsx`, `encounters/EncountersPage.jsx`
- Utils: `patientChartUtils.js`, existing `Badge` status maps in `checkoutConstants.js`

## Acceptance check

Before finishing UI work on this area: header readable in 5s; each tab has clear visual sections; status/color consistent; mobile does not horizontal-scroll except tab bar; no wall of ungrouped fields.
